explanation:
To make secant a bijection, its domain is restricted to [0,π] excluding π/2, since secant is undefined there.
So the range of sec⁻¹x is [0,π] - {π/2}.
Answer = [0,π] - {π/2}

To make cosecant a bijection, its domain is restricted to [-π/2,π/2] excluding 0, since cosecant is undefined there.
So the range of cosec⁻¹x is [-π/2,π/2] - {0}.
Answer = [-π/2,π/2] - {0}
